#[
  #set text(size: 9.0pt)
  #set par(leading: 0.63em, spacing: 0.68em)

  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Form carrying meaning is the definition. Importance of subject, oral delivery and factual accuracy are all shared with speeches, sermons and reports.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Printing is a technology, not a literary quality: ballads were literature for centuries before print, and a telephone directory is printed every year.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The test is the making of the language, not the truth of the content — which is why a memoir qualifies and a lie does not have to.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Drama, prose and poetry. The other three lists are divisions within a genre: prose, drama and prose fiction respectively.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A genre is a family defined by its mode of arrival — action, narration or compression — not by date, style or subject.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Drama arrives in action, so its evidence is theatrical: dialogue, directions, costume, exits. A narrator belongs to prose, headings to prose chapters.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Drama is action organised around desire and obstacle. Feeling belongs to lyric poetry, chronology to history, and narratorial knowledge to prose.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    You cannot interpret an image before you know what is literally happening, nor judge an arrangement before you have seen it. The order is cumulative.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It reads an image — a comparison between compound and garment — which is the figurative level.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It concerns order and withholding, which are structural. The literal level would only report that the demand is made.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Evaluation judges success and cost. The other three are the literal, figurative and structural levels in order.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Name, evidence, effect. A definition without evidence is a dictionary entry, and evidence without effect proves only that you can find things.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A statement true of thousands of texts distinguishes nothing about this one, so it cannot show that the text was read.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The effect is the only part that cannot be produced without understanding, which is why it carries the discriminating mark.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The subject is the topic; the theme is what the text says about it, and therefore needs a verb.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Tone belongs to the writer, mood to the audience. The other pairs are separate distinctions tested elsewhere.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Diction is word choice. The overall manner is style, rhythm belongs to prosody and arrangement to structure.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The persona is a constructed voice. A poem may be spoken by a corpse or a murderer, which the poet is not.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Story is chronological; plot is the text's order, including its withholdings. The gap between them is where suspense lives.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It asks you to name what is there. Definitions ask for the term's meaning; evaluation asks how well the passage works.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Effects are produced by difference within repetition: what has shifted by the third occurrence is the effect.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Passages usually build towards a statement of their concern, which falls at or near the close.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Contrastive conjunctions mark the hinge of an argument, and most tone questions sit on one side of that hinge.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A bare set and rain establish atmosphere and withhold information, which is expository work done by the set rather than the dialogue.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Only the first reports what happens. The second reads an image, the third an arrangement and the fourth judges the image's cost.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Free verse has no rhyme and shares imagery with prose, but its line breaks are chosen and carry meaning, which is what makes it poetry.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is about placement and sequence. The first is what happens, the third is detail, and the fourth is inference about attitude.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It has identified and located the device but has not said what it does, which is the part that earns the interpretive mark.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The distinction is standard: attitude on the writer's side, feeling on the audience's. The sentence uses both terms properly.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Diction concerns word choice. Sentence arrangement is syntax, length is a fact and reliability a matter of point of view.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Only the second makes a claim, and a theme must be a claim. The others are topics or settings.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Evaluation completes the set by asking how well the writing works and at what cost.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    “To emphasise” is a label that fits any repetition. An effect must name what becomes emphatic, and for whom.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Placement is a fact about the whole book. The other three are answerable from the words on the page.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A writer omits far more than he includes, and the omissions shape the reader's attention — which is why 'what is left out' is a fair exam question.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Relevance is judged against the text. A good point attached to the wrong evidence is a good point about something else.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Placement questions convert description into analysis, which is the movement from level one to level three.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Gloom describes the effect on the reader. Tone would need the writer's attitude — resigned, sardonic, accusing — which produces the gloom.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    That is the standard distinction. The remaining options confuse theme with moral, and subject with setting, plot and voice respectively.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Reading twice and locating the stem's verb tells you both what the passage does and how much answer is required.
  ]

]

